{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Marsh plants</b> — like צללים, and the alef is in place of the doubling letter, like אשר בזאו נהרים ארצו." "<b>In the covert of reed</b> — the height that is over the rivers." "<b>And in the marsh</b> — like 'its outflows' and its banks, a place of mud."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The lemma צאלים appears in Job 40:21; the comparison is to צללים with alef replacing the expected doubled consonant.", 2 "The words וגבאיו are read as 'its banks' in Aramaic sense; the comparison to בצאתיו is obscure and translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:31.032835877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}